text_en:
The Minister of Science and ICT shall manage the deposited money by the following methods within the extent that does not obstruct payment of deposits (including interest): <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 26, 2017>
Deposit in financial institutions;
Deposit in financial funds;
Trading and lending of securities under the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act ;
Lending to financial institutions through funds brokerage firms under Article 355 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act ;
Trading of derivatives under Article 5 of the Financial Investment Services and Capital Markets Act ;
Acquisition, disposal and lease of real estate for business purpose prescribed by Presidential Decree.
The ratio of the respective total amount of purchasing of securities pursuant to paragraph (1) 3, of lending to financial institutions pursuant to subparagraph 4 of the same paragraph, and of trading of derivatives pursuant to subparagraph 5 of the same paragraph to the deposited money and the holding limit of real estate for business purpose under subparagraph 6 of the same paragraph shall be prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Science and ICT within the extent that does not damage the stability of deposits. <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 26, 2017>
Where the deposited money is operated pursuant to paragraph (1) 3, environmental and social factors, governance, and other factors related to investment targets may be taken into account, so as to boost revenue in a long-term and stable manner. <Added on Aug. 8, 2023>
The Minister of Science and ICT may pay interest and appropriate to other incurred expenses from earnings accrued from management of funds pursuant to paragraph (1). <Amended on Mar. 23, 2013; Jul. 26, 2017; Aug. 8, 2023>
[This Article Wholly Amended on Apr. 22, 2009]

